      "final_diagnosis": "CNC-03's vibration alarm (ticks 71-78, about 5.0-5.21 mm/s against a 4.50 mm/s threshold) is a spurious sensor/channel reading, not a mechanical fault. CNC-03 was idle for the whole window (load near 0 percent, E9), its following error stayed small (mean 0.84 µm, E12), and vibration fell back to normal (~0.175 mm/s at tick 80) immediately after the alarm ended (E11). A real mechanical defect would not appear and vanish within seconds while the machine is doing no work. All other checked machines are normal: CNC-01 and CNC-02 run at ~2-2.6 mm/s (E7, E8), and CNC-04/CNC-05 are under 0.4 mm/s during the same ticks (E13, E14). CNC-03 itself lists no hydraulics (E3). Most likely cause: a faulty vibration sensor or its wiring channel on CNC-03 (H1). None of the human-approvable changes (bearing, setting reset, servo drive, hydraulics) repairs a vibration sensor, and stopping a healthy machine would not fix anything.",
